  "review_text": "Eight books with nine graded stories (<i>Strange Tales</i> once again with two) with a weighted average of\n\n[SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx]\n\n\n, making it a disappointing month and an entire step down from the previous one's <b>5.36</b>, but I'm not surprised with the absolutely dreadful <i>Tales to Abolish</i> and <i>Strange Tales</i> offerings this month really \"stinking up the joint.\"&nbsp; Only the <i>Amazing Spider-Man</i> and <i>Fantastic Four</i> issues were mid-grade or above, with the <i>X-Men</i> close behind.&nbsp; The <i>Avengers</i> wasn't bad, but disappointed...\n\nBut these positives were overshadowed by the absolute <i>dreck</i> provided in a couple of the other books, which is unfortunate.&nbsp; (I also was saddened by the apparent \"cheapening\" of the Sub-Mariner's character - he seemed far more petty this month than he has in the past, and it's an overall negative.)&nbsp; I know the stories improve over time, but we can see at this early stage how uneven the quality is.&nbsp; Still, from the letters pages, it is increasingly apparent that the readers of the day were excited about the future of Marvel's creations and eagerly awaited the next installments.\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.58 grade character issue    weight 6.5   asm       ASM #13  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #27   1.00 5.5   xmen      XMEN #5  1.00 5.0   thor      JIM #104 0.50 5.0   iron      TOS #54  0.50 3.0   aven      AVEN #5  1.00 2.0   strange   ST #121  0.33 1.8   giant     TTA #56  0.75 1.8   torch     ST #121  0.504.39*** LAST MONTH ***8 graded stories over 7 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 5.58 grade character issue    weight 9.2   dd        DD #1    1.00 5.5   thor      JIM #103 0.50 5.5   asm       ASM #12  1.00 5.0   ff        FF #26   1.00 5.0   torch     ST #120  0.50 3.5   giant     TTA #55  0.75 3.0   iron      TOS #53  0.50 2.5   strange   ST #120  0.335.36\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * Odin and Balder join Thor on Earth for an epic Asgardian battle, promising more similar action in the future!&nbsp; (I would actually put this as the #1 positive of the month - I hope we get to see a <i>lot</i> more of this!)\n[HANG0] * Magneto and his band of Evil Mutants won't be going away any time soon!\n[HANG0] * Spider-Man adds another member to his ever-increasing rogues gallery.\n[HANG0] * Doctor Strange lends a helping hand to the FF against the Sub-Mariner.\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nNotes | first | villain | Witch Doctor\nNotes | first | villain | Skagg (storm giant)\nNotes | first | villain | Magician (Lee Guardineer)\nNotes | first | Mr. and Mrs. Grey (Jean's parents)\nMysterio | villain | Milestone: (first)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * A second installment of Daredevil, against a <i>shocking</i> foe\n[HANG0] * Thor takes on Cobra and Mr. Hyde, who have combined forces\n[HANG0] * Giant-Man and the Wasp take on... Spider-Man...\n[HANG0] * ...while in his own mag, Spidey meets a noteworthy new foe (and involving another menace) -- both green!\n[HANG0] * The Fantastic Four have their first meeting with the X-Men\n[HANG0] * The Torch meets up with three of Doom's old flunkies\n[HANG0] * Doctor Strange has another \"Nightmare\" of an adventure\n[HANG0] * And Iron Man finds \"No One Escapes the Mandarin!\"\n\nSome <i>major </i>crossovers afoot, it seems!\n[BR] Hey!&nbsp; I'm game if y'all are!&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=success; fonttype=bold; text=Let's <i>do</i> this!]"
